 a SINGLE multiplication like 9x9 = 12 bytes BUT a matrice of 9x9 uses =972 bytes
now if we use the same math which is 2 bits per neuron and we convert 972 into a valid bit we get 7776 bits, now we divide that by 2 because 2bits per neuron  and we get 3888 Neurons and   i am planning to implement near 3k to 4k of neurons in v3.0 meaning that a single multiplication matrice of 9x9 is similar to the neuron count/usage at the MAX so then

a single multiplication e.g 9x9 = 81 so  12 bytes 
but that converted is 48 NEURONS ar the highest value (1) so this means that if random the number could be signifigantly lower to be real.

now if we take a matrice of 9x9 meaning 81 miultiplication we find that it uses  972 bytes AND more 
while in 972 we can get 7776 bits that converts to 3888 Neurons on the highest vaalue aka 1 since its ternary neurons and not binary.

this way using our simple math and conversion scale and calculation+ trajectory the RAM usage is WAY LESS and biologically closer to an actual brain and way more efficient


